# deploy/env/issuer-devnet.env: the Business Pass issuer of the LOCAL dev stack (deploy/docker-compose.dev.yml,
# docs/LOCAL.md). Copy to issuer-devnet.env (git-ignored); scripts/dev-up.sh does it for you and fills the pepper.
# PORT, CHAIN_ID, ISSUER_MOCK, CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS and REGISTRY_ADDRESS are set by docker-compose.dev.yml.
# No inline comments after values: docker compose would keep them as part of the value.
#
# THE KEY BELOW IS ANVIL'S PUBLIC TEST KEY ("test test ... junk" mnemonic, account 4). DeployLocal.s.sol makes its
# address the devnet BusinessPassRegistry issuer. Worthless anywhere else. NEVER put a Sepolia or mainnet key here.

# anvil account 4 (devnet Business Pass issuer)
ISSUER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x47e179ec197488593b187f80a00eb0da91f1b9d0b13f8733639f19c30a34926a

# Random per machine, 64 hex chars WITHOUT 0x (`openssl rand -hex 32`). dev-up writes the same value as
# BUSINESS_PEPPER in agents-devnet.env, so the Node and the Python issuer derive the same business nullifier.
ISSUER_PEPPER=
